{
  "requirement": "`ValidationCache::new()` creates an empty cache for running criteria without\nan agent.\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl<D: Domain> ValidationCache<D> {\n    pub fn new() -> Self;\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement has two obligations. `ValidationCache::new()` must create an empty cache, and the cache must be usable for running criteria without an agent.\n\n- **Unit test:** `agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[new_cache_starts_without_files_or_agent]` calls `ValidationCache::<TestDomain>::new()`. It asserts that `agent` is `None`, `sources` is `None`, and the `outlines` map is empty. That covers \"empty\" and \"without an agent\" for every field the test can reach.\n- **Contract test:** `tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_clones_share_the_first_successful_outline_for_each_path]` builds a fresh cache with `ValidationCache::<Application>::new()` and uses it with no agent. The first lookup of a missing file fails, which shows the cache starts empty. Later lookups cache and share snapshots correctly, which shows the cache works.\n- **Untested field:** the private `nodes` field in `domain.rs#struct[ValidationCache]` is not asserted empty, because it is not accessible from the unit test. A freshly built cache that passes the other empty checks has no observable way to contain pre-populated nodes. I do not count this as a gap.\n\nBoth tests carry `{test}` references to the requirement.",
  "references": "bb6fff83f12d9662bcbd1e2eb6088fd8333e94ff01a7055d64c95abde7af5e69",
